[00:08.38]At the start of the day, with the sun yet to rise,
[00:16.30]We are making our way
[00:18.70]with the sleep in our eyes, and we pray.
[00:25.06]We are there with a smile for the people we meet.
[00:33.47]Some may stop for a while,
[00:35.64]some pass by on the street, but we stay.
[00:39.91](Chorus)
[00:40.06]It’s the life that we choose;
[00:46.02]For Jehovah we live.
[00:50.40]And whatever he asks, we will do.
[00:58.88]In the work we endure,
[01:03.04]Whether sunshine or rain.
[01:07.36]It’s a way we can say ev’ry day: “I love you.”
[01:24.04]At the end of the day, with the sun sinking low,
[01:31.88]Feeling happy and tired,
[01:34.78]in our heart there’s a glow, and we pray.
[01:40.97]It’s a life that we love, always giving our best.
[01:48.86]And Jehovah we thank,
[01:51.54]for by him we are blessed ev’ry day.
[01:55.77](Chorus)
[01:55.92]It’s the life that we choose;
[02:01.94]For Jehovah we live.
[02:06.22]And whatever he asks, we will do.
[02:14.66]In the work we endure,
[02:18.88]Whether sunshine or rain.
[02:22.70]It’s a way we can say ev’ry day: “I love you.”
